dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.image.mutations
version 1
schema s.stdio.semio.image
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION image wave: REAL binary op frame,
# replacing the old `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioImageMutation` is a genuine
# data-carrying enum whose `SetSnapshot` variant embeds a nested `SemioImageSnapshot` payload — no
# `dsl::DslField` impl exists for it (hand-rolled per this subset's own `📸️snapshot`/`🔺️diff`
# convention, `icc: Option<Vec<u8>>` being a bare-`Option` field the derive machinery cannot bind),
# so the generic derive-based `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout doesn't apply.
# Handcrafted instead: `format u8` (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the
# `SemioImageMutation` variant ordinal, `🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/
# `variant_ordinal`, 0-12 matching `parse_image_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed
# fields, then the variant's own argument payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — the same
# honest boundary the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` uses.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
